  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 145 PM CDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nWednesday night through Monday:\n\nWeak cold advection is expected Wed nt followed by a broad sfc \nridge on Thu. A shortwave trough will also pass on Thu but the \nairmass is too dry for many clouds or rain. Sly winds and warm, \nmoist advection will return for Fri ahead of a weak shortwave \ntrough, which will pass Fri nt. There are 30-50 percent chances \nfor showers Fri nt then 20-30 percent Sat AM with the cold \nfrontal passage. \n\nMore substantial cyclogenesis is then possible Sun nt into Mon\nfrom the central Great Plains into the nrn Great Lakes. There \nare 40-50 percent chances for showers and storms during this\ntime. Temperatures from mid week into early next week will be\nnear seasonal normals. \n\nGehring",
